QEMU V3D test model (DARW-295)
==============================

bcm2835_v3d.[ch] are a test model of the VideoCore IV 3D block for the
qemu-zhuowei fork's raspi3 machine (ASB bridges, PM_GRAFX, V3D registers,
interrupts, job completion, hang injection, clear-only job emulation).
install.py copies them into third_party/qemu-zhuowei and wires them in
(Makefile.objs, bcm2835_peripherals.[ch], bcm2835_powermgt.[ch], the
mailbox "set clock state" tag). Idempotent; then build with tools/build_qemu.sh.

THIS DIRECTORY IS A STAND-IN. Per the repo rule the change belongs committed
in the anurodhp/qemu-zhuowei fork; it was made in that fork's working tree from
a session that could not commit there, so the sources are kept here until
someone commits them to the fork (then delete this directory).

Tests: tools/v3d_qemu_probe.sh (QEMU_DTB=devicetrees/rpi3-v3dtest.dtb),
tools/v3d_qemu_hang_test.sh. Properties: -global bcm2835-v3d.hang-job=N
-global bcm2835-v3d.hang-thread=0|1 -global bcm2835-powermgt.grafx-boot-powered=off.
It models the driver's own assumptions (written from the same Linux sources),
so it checks plumbing and driver logic, not hardware truth.
